    "result_text": "Tests are green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI agreed with the finding and addressed it. The inbound `title` enum\u2192`String` conversion was being done inline in `updateOwner` while the create path relied on MapStruct's implicit enum\u2192String conversion \u2014 two different mechanisms in two places, inconsistent with how `normalizeTelephone`/`normalizeEmail`/`applyAddressFields` centralize inbound transformations in the mapper.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Named(\"mapTitle\")` default method that unwraps `OwnerFieldsDto.TitleEnum` to its canonical `String` value (or `null`), with Javadoc matching its siblings. Made the conversion explicit on `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` via `@Mapping(target = \"title\", source = \"title\", qualifiedByName = \"mapTitle\")` instead of relying on an implicit built-in conversion.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.updateOwner`** \u2014 Now calls `ownerMapper.mapTitle(ownerFieldsDto.getTitle())`, the same pattern as the adjacent `normalizeTelephone`/`normalizeEmail` calls.\n\nBoth create and update now share one definition of the inbound `title` mapping, restoring create/update symmetry. The acceptance test (`coreComposesSalutation`) and the full suite remain green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
