        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe new `formatSalutation` method itself is clean and idiomatic \u2014 it sits right alongside its `formatDisplayName`/`formatInitials` siblings, follows the identical `@Named` + `qualifiedByName` pattern, has a matching Javadoc, and the Owner entity / schema / OpenAPI additions are all consistent with the surrounding code. My concern is with where the inbound `title` conversion was placed.\n\n**Finding \u2014 title enum\u2192String conversion is in the wrong unit and is applied asymmetrically between the create and update paths.**\n\n`OwnerRestControllerV1.updateOwner` (line 164) does the conversion inline:\n\n```java\ncurrentOwner.setTitle(ownerFieldsDto.getTitle() == null ? null : ownerFieldsDto.getTitle().getValue());\n```\n\nThis diverges from the established convention in this controller/mapper pair:\n\n- Every other field that needs a *transformation* on the way in is routed through an `OwnerMapper` method (`normalizeTelephone`, `normalizeEmail`, and the structured-address logic in `applyAddressFields`). Only trivial pass-through fields (`firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `postcode`) are set directly in the controller. The `title` unwrap is a non-trivial type conversion (enum \u2192 `String`), so by the local convention it belongs in the mapper, not inline in the controller.\n- The create path (`addOwner`) builds the owner via `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)` and never runs this inline logic. `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (lines 305\u2013312) has no mapping entry for `title`, so the two paths handle `title` in two different places by two different mechanisms. That asymmetry is exactly the kind of thing a maintainer later has to reconcile, and it's the same consistency problem that `applyAddressFields` was explicitly written to avoid (\"called directly on the update path to keep both create and update consistent\").\n\nSuggested fix: move the enum-unwrapping into `OwnerMapper` so both paths share one definition \u2014 e.g. a `@Named(\"mapTitle\")` default method taking the DTO's title enum and returning the `String`, referenced by an explicit `@Mapping(target = \"title\", ...)` on `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` and called from `updateOwner` the same way `normalizeTelephone`/`normalizeEmail` are. That keeps the inbound `title` mapping in a single unit alongside the other field normalizations and restores create/update symmetry."
